---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test: $GET locals\n; Tests retrieving values from local B-tree variables\n\n; Set up test data\n$SET x = 42\n$SET items(1) = \"first\"\n$SET items(2) = \"second\"\n$SET patient(123, \"name\") = \"John\"\n$SET patient(123, \"age\") = 30\n\n; $GET simple local\nLET val = $GET x\n$OUTPUT val\n; Expected: 42 (or Option.Some(42))\n\n; $GET with subscript\nLET d1 = $GET items(1)\n$OUTPUT d1\n; Expected: first\n\nLET d2 = $GET items(2)\n$OUTPUT d2\n; Expected: second\n\n; $GET with multiple subscripts\nLET name = $GET patient(123, \"name\")\n$OUTPUT name\n; Expected: John\n\nLET age = $GET patient(123, \"age\")\n$OUTPUT age\n; Expected: 30\n\n; $GET non-existent key (should return Option.None)\nLET missing = $GET items(999)\n$OUTPUT missing\n; Expected: Option.None (or similar)\n\nLET missing2 = $GET nonexistent\n$OUTPUT missing2\n; Expected: Option.None\n\n; $GET after overwrite\n$SET x = 100\nLET newval = $GET x\n$OUTPUT newval\n; Expected: 100\n\n$OUTPUT \"$GET locals test complete\"\n"
---
Option.Some(42)
Option.Some("first")
Option.Some("second")
Option.Some("John")
Option.Some(30)
Option.None
Option.None
Option.Some(100)
"$GET locals test complete"
